    "file": "langfuse/_client/span_exporter.py",
    "line": 348,
    "failure_mode": "Spans that have a patch returned by mask_otel_spans are appended without applying the patch due to inverted condition (checking patch is not None to skip further processing), while spans without a patch fall through to patch-application logic with patch=None.",
    "impact": "Patched attributes are silently not applied, and unpatched spans may be processed by code expecting a patch, potentially causing incorrect attribute mutations or errors. This breaks the masking contract and results in incorrect data export.",
    "suggested_fix": "Restore the original condition so that spans without a patch are appended as-is and patched spans proceed to have their patch applied. Specifically, change `if patch is not None:` back to `if patch is None:` so patched spans go through the patch-application code path."
  }
]

